module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.DenseSubsiteModules
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.IdealPresentationSite
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The global augmented complex `K^• ⟶ 𝒪` of [Stacks, Tag 099E]

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` a sheaf of ideals of finite type. On the presentation
site `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IdealPres` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/DerivedCompletionRinged/IdealPresentationSite.lean`
the complex `K^•` of [Stacks, Tag 099D] is a complex of presheaves of modules with no choice of
generators anywhere, `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presCechComplex`, and the forgetful functor to
`𝒞` is a dense subsite. This file cashes that in:

* sheafify `K^•` degreewise on the presentation site, and
* transport the result to `𝒞` along the Comparison Lemma for sheaves of modules,
  `Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestrictionEquivalence`.

The outcome is a complex of sheaves of `𝒪`-modules on `𝒞` together with an augmentation onto the
structure sheaf, hence a map `K^• ⟶ 𝒪` of `D(𝒪)`. This is the object whose existence
[Stacks, Tag 099E] asserts; what that tag asserts *about* it — that its restriction to a slice
over an object where `ℐ` is generated by `f_1, …, f_r` is the extended alternating Čech complex
of `f`, compatibly with the augmentations — is not proved here.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presTopology`: the topology on the presentation site for which a
  sieve covers exactly when its image in `𝒞` does.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presRingSheaf`: the structure sheaf of rings restricted to the
  presentation site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presSheafComplex` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presSheafAugmentation`: the degreewise sheafification of `K^•` on
  the presentation site, and its augmentation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleEquivIdealPres`: the Comparison Lemma for sheaves of
  modules at the presentation site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalCechComplex` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalCechAugmentation`: **the complex `K^•` of
  [Stacks, Tag 099E] on `𝒞` and its augmentation onto `𝒪`**.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalCechObject` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalCechMap`: the same read in `D(𝒪)`, as a map `K ⟶ 𝒪`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isCoverDense_idealPresForget_of_isFiniteType` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDenseSubsite_idealPresForget_of_isFiniteType`: the hypotheses
  of the presentation site's dense-subsite statement are supplied by
  `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, through
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleRestriction_globalCechComplex`: **the restriction of the
  global complex to the presentation site is the sheafified `K^•`** — the sense in which the
  global complex is the one built from the choice-free presheaf complex.

## Implementation notes

Everything is stated at `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.{u, u, u}`. The reason is the hypothesis
`HasLimitsOfShape (StructuredArrow Y G.op) AddCommGrpCat.{w}` of Mathlib's Comparison Lemma,
exactly as for `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleEquivFinitelyGeneratedLocus`: the
structured-arrow categories of the forgetful functor are indexed by the objects and arrows of
`𝒞`, so the coefficient universe must contain both. At `{u, u, u}` the presentation site is a
`Type u` with `Type u` of arrows, and then sheafification for `AddCommGrpCat.{u}` on it — and the
condition `GrothendieckTopology.WEqualsLocallyBijective` — are found by instance search with no
hypothesis, so the construction carries no sheafification hypothesis of its own.

The dense-subsite datum is introduced with `letI` rather than as an instance argument, so that
the global complex depends on the finite-type hypothesis only, and on nothing a caller has to
supply. `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsDenseSubsite` is a proposition, so the resulting data is
well defined.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. [Stacks, Tag 099E] is the conjunction of the existence of
`K ⟶ 𝒪` and the Čech identification on every slice where `ℐ` is finitely generated; only the
first is here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DG)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

section Global

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **The topology on the presentation site**: a sieve covers exactly when its image in `𝒞`
generates a covering sieve. -/
abbrev presTopology : GrothendieckTopology (IdealPres 𝓘) :=
  (idealPresForget 𝓘).restrictedTopology X.J

variable (h : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType)

include h

/-- **The forgetful functor from the presentation site of a finite-type sheaf of ideals is cover
dense.** The covering family of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType` supplies
the hypothesis of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isCoverDense_idealPresForget`. -/
theorem isCoverDense_idealPresForget_of_isFiniteType :
    (idealPresForget 𝓘).IsCoverDense X.J := by
  obtain ⟨ι, V, hV, r, f, hf⟩ := exists_coversTop_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType 𝓘 h
  exact isCoverDense_idealPresForget 𝓘 hV fun i ↦ ⟨r i, f i, hf i⟩

/-- **The presentation site of a finite-type sheaf of ideals is a dense subsite of `(𝒞, J)`.** -/
theorem isDenseSubsite_idealPresForget_of_isFiniteType :
    (idealPresForget 𝓘).IsDenseSubsite (presTopology X 𝓘) X.J :=
  let := isCoverDense_idealPresForget_of_isFiniteType X 𝓘 h
  let := isLocallyFull_idealPresForget 𝓘
  inferInstance

/-- **The structure sheaf of rings restricted to the presentation site.** -/
def presRingSheaf : Sheaf (presTopology X 𝓘) RingCat.{u} :=
  letI := isDenseSubsite_idealPresForget_of_isFiniteType X 𝓘 h
  Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.ringRestriction (presTopology X 𝓘) X.J
    (idealPresForget 𝓘) ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))

/-- The restricted sheaf of rings has, as its underlying presheaf, the restriction of the
structure presheaf along the forgetful functor. -/
theorem presRingSheaf_obj :
    (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h).obj =
      (idealPresForget 𝓘).op ⋙ ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj := rfl

/-- The identity of the restricted structure presheaf is locally injective, which is one of the
two hypotheses `PresheafOfModules.sheafification` takes on its scalar comparison. It is an
instance of `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_injective` at the identity. -/
instance isLocallyInjective_id_presRingSheaf :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective (presTopology X 𝓘) (𝟙 (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h).obj) :=
  Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_injective _ _ fun _ _ _ hxy ↦ hxy

/-- The identity of the restricted structure presheaf is locally surjective. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_id_presRingSheaf :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (presTopology X 𝓘) (𝟙 (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h).obj) :=
  Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_surjective _ _ fun _ x ↦ ⟨x, rfl⟩

/-- **The sheafification functor for presheaves of modules on the presentation site.** -/
abbrev presSheafification :
    PresheafOfModules.{u} (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h).obj ⥤
      SheafOfModules.{u} (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h) :=
  PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h).obj)

/-- Sheafification of presheaves of modules on the presentation site is an additive functor. -/
instance additive_presSheafification : (presSheafification X 𝓘 h).Additive :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction
    (𝟙 (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h).obj)).left_adjoint_additive

/-- **The degreewise sheafification on the presentation site of the choice-free complex `K^•`**
of [Stacks, Tag 099D]. -/
abbrev presSheafComplex : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h)) ℕ :=
  ((presSheafification X 𝓘 h).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).obj
    (presCechComplex 𝓘)

/-- **The augmentation of the sheafified `K^•` onto the structure sheaf of the presentation
site.** It is the sheafification of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presCechAugmentation` followed
by the counit of the sheafification adjunction at the structure sheaf, which is already a
sheaf. -/
def presSheafAugmentation :
    (presSheafComplex X 𝓘 h).X 0 ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h) :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationHomEquiv
    (𝟙 (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h).obj)).symm (presCechAugmentation 𝓘)

/-- **The Comparison Lemma for sheaves of modules at the presentation site**: sheaves of
`𝒪`-modules on `𝒞` are the same as sheaves of modules over the restricted structure sheaf on the
presentation site. -/
def moduleEquivIdealPres :
    SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ≌
      SheafOfModules.{u} (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h) :=
  letI := isDenseSubsite_idealPresForget_of_isFiniteType X 𝓘 h
  Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestrictionEquivalence (presTopology X 𝓘) X.J
    (idealPresForget 𝓘) ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))

/-- The Comparison Lemma's forward direction, restriction of sections, is additive: it carries a
morphism of sheaves of modules to the morphism with the same components, and addition of
morphisms is componentwise. -/
instance additive_moduleEquivIdealPres_functor :
    (moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).functor.Additive where
  map_add := rfl

/-- The inverse direction of the Comparison Lemma, from sheaves of modules on the presentation
site to sheaves of `𝒪`-modules on `𝒞`, is an additive functor. -/
instance additive_moduleEquivIdealPres_inverse :
    (moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).inverse.Additive :=
  (moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).toAdjunction.right_adjoint_additive

/-- **The complex `K^•` of [Stacks, Tag 099E] on `𝒞`**: the degreewise sheafification on the
presentation site of the choice-free complex of [Stacks, Tag 099D], transported to `𝒞` by the
Comparison Lemma. -/
def globalCechComplex :
    CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ℕ :=
  (((moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).inverse).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).obj
    (presSheafComplex X 𝓘 h)

/-- **The restriction of the global complex to the presentation site is the sheafified `K^•`.**
This is the sense in which `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalCechComplex` is built from the
choice-free presheaf complex: the Comparison Lemma's forward direction is restriction of
sections, and its counit identifies the restriction of the transported complex with the
original one, degreewise and compatibly with the differentials. -/
def moduleRestriction_globalCechComplex :
    ((moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).functor.mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).obj
        (globalCechComplex X 𝓘 h) ≅
      presSheafComplex X 𝓘 h :=
  HomologicalComplex.Hom.isoOfComponents
    (fun n ↦ (moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).counitIso.app ((presSheafComplex X 𝓘 h).X n))
    fun _ _ _ ↦ ((moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).counitIso.hom.naturality _).symm

/-- The structure sheaf of the presentation site is the restriction of the structure sheaf of
`𝒞`, as a sheaf of modules over itself. -/
theorem functor_obj_unit :
    (moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).functor.obj
        (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) =
      SheafOfModules.unit (presRingSheaf X 𝓘 h) := rfl

/-- **The augmentation `K^• ⟶ 𝒪` of [Stacks, Tag 099E] on `𝒞`**, obtained from the augmentation
on the presentation site by the Comparison Lemma. -/
def globalCechAugmentation :
    (globalCechComplex X 𝓘 h).X 0 ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) :=
  (moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).inverse.map (presSheafAugmentation X 𝓘 h) ≫
    (moduleEquivIdealPres X 𝓘 h).unitIso.inv.app
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))

/-- **The complex `K^•` of [Stacks, Tag 099E] in `ℤ`-indexed form**, extended by zero in
negative degrees, which is the shape the derived category of `𝒞` is built from. -/
abbrev globalCechComplexInt :
    CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ℤ :=
  (globalCechComplex X 𝓘 h).extend ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat

/-- **The augmentation `K^• ⟶ 𝒪[0]` of [Stacks, Tag 099E]**, as a map of `ℤ`-indexed complexes
of sheaves of `𝒪`-modules: the augmentation of the degree-zero term in degree zero, and zero
elsewhere, the complex being concentrated in nonnegative degrees. -/
def globalCechAugmentationInt :
    globalCechComplexInt X 𝓘 h ⟶ structureSheafComplex X :=
  HomologicalComplex.mkHomToSingle
    (((globalCechComplex X 𝓘 h).extendXIso ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat
      (i := 0) (i' := 0) rfl).hom ≫ globalCechAugmentation X 𝓘 h)
    fun i hi ↦ by
      obtain rfl : i = -1 := by
        have : i + 1 = 0 := hi
        omega
      exact ((globalCechComplex X 𝓘 h).isZero_extend_X ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat (-1)
        (fun n hn ↦ by simp only [ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat_f] at hn; omega)).eq_of_src _ 0

/-- **The object `K` of `D(𝒪)` whose existence [Stacks, Tag 099E] asserts.** -/
abbrev globalCechObject :
    DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :=
  DerivedCategory.Q.obj (globalCechComplexInt X 𝓘 h)

/-- **The map `K ⟶ 𝒪` of `D(𝒪)` whose existence [Stacks, Tag 099E] asserts.** What that tag
asserts about it — the Čech identification on every slice where `ℐ` is generated by finitely many
sections, compatibly with the maps to `𝒪_U` — is not proved here. -/
def globalCechMap :
    globalCechObject X 𝓘 h ⟶ DerivedCategory.Q.obj (structureSheafComplex X) :=
  DerivedCategory.Q.map (globalCechAugmentationInt X 𝓘 h)

end Global

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
